# Six hundred numbers written by ICU 79.1 (CLDR 49), the reference this
# package's writer is held to: each line a locale, a style, a number, a
# currency and what ICU wrote, separated by tabs. Drawn at random
# (seed 11) from 6,570 cases, ten for each of CLDR 49's 657 locales, run
# through ICU on 2026-11-19 by a one-off program, which is not in the tree
# (defect 2639), its styles `unum_open` with CLDR's minimum grouping for
# decimals, percentages and scientific numbers and `NumberFormatter` for money
# and compact numbers. The 140 cases of locales ICU does not carry, which it
# writes as the root writes them, are left out, and so are en-GE and en-HU,
# whose euros ICU writes before the number where CLDR's data writes them after
# it. Only a test build reads the cases.

use i18n
use i18n/numbers/internal/formatting
use strings

# The cases.
constant CASES: [str]
    [
        "af\tdecimal\t100\t\t100"
        "af\tpercent\t999999\t\t99 999 900%"
        "ak\tcompact_short\t-1234567.891\t\t-1.2M"
        "am\tdecimal\t-1\t\t-1"
